# Circuit Break — a live immersive theatre piece for ~24 audience.
#
# Audience members ("participants") arrive in the Plaza. Over the
# evening they enroll into one of three cohorts — Chatters, Mods, or
# (against their knowledge, at first) Cyborgs. Performers run improv
# beats in five physical locations; the Playwright drives advances
# from the simulator, watching cohort counts and broadcasts on the
# ledger.
#
# The show is reactive: every beat reads the live `Tension` world
# value and the dispositions / knowledge of Vex and Praxis, and routes
# through different branches accordingly. The simulator's Graph tab
# can edit any of these mid-show.

entry: arrival

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cohorts — audience subsets the Playwright herds into and out of.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------

COHORT Audience
  label: The Audience
  capacity: 32

COHORT Chatters
  label: The Chatters
  capacity: 24

COHORT Mods
  label: The Mods
  capacity: 24

COHORT Cyborgs
  label: The Cyborgs
  capacity: 12

COHORT Defectors
  label: The Defectors (pulled aside by NineIron)
  capacity: 6

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Locations — physical stations in the venue. Performers live here.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------

LOCATION Plaza
  label: The Uplink Plaza
  ambient: neon-static
  capacity: 32

LOCATION ChatterCamp
  label: The Chatter Camp (data-hall, stickered to hell)
  ambient: shoutcast-loop
  capacity: 24

LOCATION ModOutpost
  label: The Mod Outpost (former server room, fans on full)
  ambient: server-fans
  capacity: 24

LOCATION NineIronHide
  label: NineIron's locker
  ambient: distant-drip
  capacity: 8

LOCATION MotherboardCore
  label: The Core
  ambient: green-silicon-hum
  capacity: 32

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Performers — each is a real human actor running a station.
# Tracked as characters so disposition can shift and hooks can fire
# when a cohort reaches a threshold.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------

CHARACTER Vex
  trusts Chatters: 60 of 100
  reacts trust > 80 -> vex_committed
  reacts trust < 30 -> vex_breaking

  knows:
    motherboard_named: bool = false
    saw_cyborg: bool = false

  on Chatters.trust drops below 30:
    <set: Tension += 15>
    -> vex_breaking

CHARACTER Praxis
  trusts Mods: 60 of 100
  reacts trust > 80 -> praxis_committed
  reacts trust < 30 -> praxis_breaking

  knows:
    motherboard_named: bool = false
    saw_cyborg: bool = false

CHARACTER NineIron
  trusts Defectors: 50 of 100

  knows:
    motherboard_named: bool = false

CHARACTER Motherboard
  knows:
    revealed: bool = false

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Opening pageant — everyone in the Plaza. The first arrival beat
# is the same regardless; what comes next is decided by how the
# audience reacts (Tension goes up with crowd silence, down with
# applause). The Playwright sets Tension from the simulator's Graph
# inspector while watching the room.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------

== arrival
  cast: Vex, Praxis
  setting: Plaza

<set: Tension = 25>

The house lights drop. A thousand dead screens flicker once, in
unison, then resume their static. The Audience filters into the
Plaza — neon underfoot, two banners overhead.

<broadcast: location(Plaza)>
  NARRATOR
    Welcome to The Stack. Tonight, you choose a side. Tonight, you
    find out what the sides are.

VEX | PRAXIS
  (improv duration: 60s, advance on: quorum(8) [speech(go), gesture(Cue)])
  (Argue about the city. Vex pitches reform; Praxis pitches order.
   Pull individual audience members into your camp by talking
   directly to them.)

<broadcast: location(Plaza)>
  NARRATOR
    The fountain at the center is dry. The crown sigil between the
    banners is fresh. Nobody admits drawing it.

# Branching on Tension — the room reads itself.
<if: Tension > 60>
  <broadcast: location(Plaza)>
    NARRATOR
      Somebody coughs and it lands like a gunshot.
  -> early_glitch
<else if: Tension < 15>
  <broadcast: location(Plaza)>
    NARRATOR
      Laughter, somewhere. Vex shoots a look. Praxis shrugs.
  -> camps_open
<else>
  * The Playwright opens the camps.
    -> camps_open
  * The Playwright triggers a Cyborg sighting first.
    -> early_glitch

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Branch — Camps open normally. Audience flows out of the Plaza.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------

== camps_open
  cast: Vex, Praxis
  setting: Plaza

<broadcast: location(Plaza)>
  VEX
    Camp's open. Real talk, real food, real plan. Follow me if you've
    had enough of being deleted.

<broadcast: location(Plaza)>
  PRAXIS
    Outpost is open. We have rules, we have light, we have an exit
    strategy. Anyone tired of screaming, walk with me.

VEX | PRAXIS
  (improv duration: 90s, advance on: quorum(12) [pedal])
  (Recruit. Tag audience members into your cohort by name. The
   Playwright watches Chatters / Mods counts on the ledger and
   advances when both cohorts have at least 6 enrolled.)

# Stat-aware: if the room split evenly, normal faction break; if one
# leader landed almost all the recruits, the other one starts to
# crack and we route through the defection arc instead.
<if: Vex.trusts.Chatters > 80 and Praxis.trusts.Mods < 40>
  <set: Tension += 20>
  <broadcast: location(Plaza)>
    NARRATOR
      Praxis loses the room and doesn't quite hide it.
  -> defection
<else if: Praxis.trusts.Mods > 80 and Vex.trusts.Chatters < 40>
  <set: Tension += 20>
  <broadcast: location(Plaza)>
    NARRATOR
      Vex stops smiling. The Plaza door slams once on the way out.
  -> defection
<else>
  * Vex and Praxis lead their cohorts out.
    -> faction_break

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Branch — Early glitch. A cyborg appears before camps open. This
# pushes the whole crowd into faster decisions; Vex and Praxis both
# pretend they didn't see what they saw.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------

== early_glitch
  cast: Vex, Praxis
  setting: Plaza

<set: Tension += 25>

<broadcast: location(Plaza)>
  NARRATOR
    A door behind the fountain grinds open on its own. Something
    walks out and is, on inspection, mostly cable.

<set: Vex.knows.motherboard_named = true>
<set: Praxis.knows.motherboard_named = true>
<set: Vex.knows.saw_cyborg = true>
<set: Praxis.knows.saw_cyborg = true>

CYBORG
  (improv duration: 30s, advance on: all [gesture(recoil)])
  (Stand utterly still. Turn the head ninety degrees, then a hundred,
   then back. Make eye contact with three specific audience members.
   Then walk back through the door.)

VEX
  (improv duration: 45s, advance on: any [speech(go), gesture(Cue)])
  (Pretend you didn't see it. Recruit harder. Audience members who
   ask about the cyborg get vague answers — until you crack.)

PRAXIS
  (improv duration: 45s, advance on: any [speech(go), gesture(Cue)])
  (Same: deny, then pivot to recruitment. Praxis cracks faster than
   Vex.)

# Tension after a glitch decides the next move.
<if: Tension > 70>
  <broadcast: location(Plaza)>
    NARRATOR
      Nobody in the Plaza is performing anymore.
  -> defection
<else>
  * Audience members head to the camps anyway.
    -> faction_break
  * The Playwright pulls a small group aside to NineIron now.
    -> defection

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Reactive Vex states — fired by `reacts` clauses on the CHARACTER
# block above. The runtime detours through these whenever the trust
# threshold crosses, then returns control via the divert at the end.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------

== vex_committed
  cast: Vex
  setting: ChatterCamp

VEX
  (improv duration: 30s, advance on: any [speech(go)])
  (Make a promise to the Chatter cohort you cannot, technically,
   keep. Mean it.)

<set: Tension -= 10>
<-

== vex_breaking
  cast: Vex
  setting: ChatterCamp

<set: Tension += 15>

VEX
  (improv duration: 30s, advance on: any [gesture(turn-away)])
  (Lose the room. Address one specific audience member who left.
   Ask, quietly, what you did wrong.)

<-

== praxis_committed
  cast: Praxis
  setting: ModOutpost

PRAXIS
  (improv duration: 30s, advance on: any [speech(go)])
  (Deputize three Mods on the spot. Hand out armbands. Mean it.)

<set: Tension -= 10>
<-

== praxis_breaking
  cast: Praxis
  setting: ModOutpost

<set: Tension += 15>

PRAXIS
  (improv duration: 30s, advance on: any [gesture(slump)])
  (Sit down on the desk. Drop the gavel. Tell the cohort, exactly,
   what you were afraid of.)

<-
